  "schema": "semio.framework.server.wire/v1",
  "note": "🔌️ The language-agnostic wire contract of the server product: the gateway's own route table, and one canonical JSON document per wire type. Rust (🧪️tests/🔬️wire/🦀️.rs) and TypeScript (🟦️.ts) each deserialize every vector into their own twin and serialize it back, asserting the result equals this document. A rename on either side fails the other side's suite. Field spellings are deliberate and not all camelCase: traceContext and frontierSummary carry no serde rename, and an internally tagged enum renames its variants but never the fields inside them, which is why commandOutcome carries canonical_events and rejection carries command_kind. Every route names the group it is mounted with: core is always mounted, ephemeral, blobs and apps only by an instance that asks for them, documents only by an instance that hosts a document authority. The error table is every error the gateway answers with: its status and the kind tag of its errorBody; throttled and overloaded carry retryAfterMs and a Retry-After header.",
